The text towers of SigLIP 2 B/16 and PE core B/16 with their weights in 8 bits, as whenframe downloads them from
its release models-2 (https://github.com/qthullie/whenframe/releases/tag/models-2)

SigLIP 2, by Google: https://github.com/google-research/big_vision
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The text tower was read from onnx-community's ONNX export of
google/siglip2-base-patch16-224 (onnx-community/siglip2-base-patch16-224-ONNX, revision ba1f3b08).

Perception Encoder, PE core B/16, by Meta: https://github.com/facebookresearch/perception_models
Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The text tower was read from onnx-community's ONNX export of
PE core B/16 in float16 (onnx-community/PE-Core-B16-224-ONNX, revision 7668f1df).

whenframe changed how the weights are stored, not the towers' graphs: scripts/text8.py compresses each weight
matrix to 8 bits with NNCF (one scale and zero point per output channel) and saves the tower for OpenVINO
(siglip2-base-text-int8.xml and .bin, pe-core-b16-text-int8.xml and .bin). The Apache License, Version 2.0, is in
text-int8-LICENSE.txt, next to this file.
